### Configure and Query Claude with Agent Skills (Python/TypeScript)

Source: https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/skills

This example demonstrates how to initialize the Claude Agent SDK for use with Agent Skills. It shows how to configure `ClaudeAgentOptions` (Python) or `options` (TypeScript) by specifying the current working directory (`cwd`), setting `setting_sources` or `settingSources` to load skills from the filesystem, and including `"Skill"` in the `allowed_tools` array. The code then performs an asynchronous query using the configured options, allowing Claude to discover and invoke relevant skills.

```python
import asyncio
from claude_agent_sdk import query, ClaudeAgentOptions

async def main():
    options = ClaudeAgentOptions(
        cwd="/path/to/project",  # Project with .claude/skills/
        setting_sources=["user", "project"],  # Load Skills from filesystem
        allowed_tools=["Skill", "Read", "Write", "Bash"]  # Enable Skill tool
    )

    async for message in query(
        prompt="Help me process this PDF document",
        options=options
    ):
        print(message)

asyncio.run(main())
```

